import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 437 | Dragon Ball · Retcon-Ending Deep Analysis: GT/Super/Heroes Multi-Line Contradictions","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 437 | Dragon Ball · Retcon-Ending Deep Analysis: GT/Super/Heroes Multi-Line Contradictions","no":437,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Retcon","Abrupt Ending","Dragon Ball GT","Dragon Ball Super","Dragon Ball Heroes"],"related":["27-Anchor Calibration and Maintenance","49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances","40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0437_模块2-龙珠-吃书烂尾深度分析-GT超英雄多线矛盾.md","filePath":"en/0437_模块2-龙珠-吃书烂尾深度分析-GT超英雄多线矛盾.md"}'),a={name:"en/0437_模块2-龙珠-吃书烂尾深度分析-GT超英雄多线矛盾.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,c,d){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-437-dragon-ball-·-retcon-ending-deep-analysis-gt-super-heroes-multi-line-contradictions" tabindex="-1">Entry 437 | Dragon Ball · Retcon-Ending Deep Analysis: GT/Super/Heroes Multi-Line Contradictions <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-437-dragon-ball-·-retcon-ending-deep-analysis-gt-super-heroes-multi-line-contradictions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 437 | Dragon Ball · Retcon-Ending Deep Analysis: GT/Super/Heroes Multi-Line Contradictions&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 6) | Benchmark base: Documents 27, 49, 40</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-one-ip-has-three-endings" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when one IP has three endings <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-one-ip-has-three-endings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when one IP has three endings&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The greatest tragedy of a long-running IP is not being unable to continue, but &quot;writing too successfully, forced to continue.&quot; Dragon Ball is this tragedy&#39;s global specimen: Toriyama&#39;s original ended at the Majin Buu arc; thereafter Toei&#39;s fan-sequel GT, Shueisha&#39;s official sequel Super, game-spinoff animation Heroes — three timelines, three transformation systems, three cosmologies mutually contradictory; fans still argue today &quot;which is canon.&quot; This entry takes the <strong>law-first axiom</strong> as core, deeply analyzing Dragon Ball multi-line retcon&#39;s structural lesion.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Multi-line retcon itself is energy waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Creative resources repeatedly invested</strong>: GT&#39;s SSJ4, Super&#39;s Super Saiyan God, Heroes&#39;s Kaioken + Super Saiyan Blue stacking; three systems independently developed; reader cognitive burden extremely heavy</li><li><strong>Fan energy internal friction</strong>: fans spend on &quot;which of GT and Super is canon&quot; far exceeds on the work itself</li><li><strong>Goku image split</strong>: GT&#39;s Goku turned back into a child, Super&#39;s Goku turned back into a martial artist, Heroes&#39;s Goku turned into a game character — same protagonist across three lines with completely different personality, ability, goals</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How multi-line retcon feeds civilizational regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Canon right monopolized by capital</strong>: which line counts as canon, not by law self-consistency, but by which sells best — this is law-tier &quot;plot kidnaps setting&quot;</li><li><strong>Setting flips with market</strong>: GT originally Toei fan work; after Super came out, officially &quot;soft-denied&quot;; Heroes even more cross-temporal crashing, pulling all previous villains back to fight again</li><li><strong>Reader trust overdrawn</strong>: when readers find &quot;no line counts,&quot; the worldview&#39;s historical feel completely collapses — Dragon Ball world in fans&#39; hearts already has no &quot;history,&quot; only &quot;latest work&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking under multi-line retcon:</p><ul><li><strong>Cross-timeline predation</strong>: Heroes pulls GT, Super, original-work villains all into one timeline; Goku fights through each across three timelines — Myriad Ranks die once per timeline</li><li><strong>Classic characters&#39; devalued use</strong>: Frieza, Cell, Buu these already &quot;curtseyed&quot; villains, repeatedly pulled back for reuse; their story completeness narratively plundered</li><li><strong>Childhood nostalgia consumption</strong>: Goku turned back into child (GT), Goku back to martial artist (Super), Goku cross-temporal fighting (Heroes) — every work consumes fans&#39; childhood nostalgia, not building new civilization</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dragon Ball Multi-Line Retcon</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Law-First Plan</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Three works contradictory, canon right by market</td><td>Law-first axiom: law precedes, never retcon; setting self-consistency above plot convenience</td></tr><tr><td>Villains repeatedly pulled back</td><td>Symbiotic Court judicial independence: villain disposition closed once; no revival, no soft-change</td></tr><tr><td>Protagonist image split</td><td>Anchor Council legislation: protagonist positioning written into constitution first; not drifting with market</td></tr><tr><td>Timeline chaos</td><td>Alaya Network archive: civilizational history has unique authoritative record; no multi-line parallel</td></tr><tr><td>Nostalgia consumption</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republican co-build: IP expansion via &quot;appendix increment&quot;; do not overturn old setting</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball three works&#39; timelines — original Buu-arc ending, GT ending, Super ending</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;if Toriyama did not write sequels after Buu arc ended&quot; control; observe IP&#39;s completeness in fans&#39; hearts</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count &quot;setting items mutually contradictory across three works,&quot; &quot;fan canon-right dispute volume&quot;</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Dragon Ball Multi-Line Retcon Loss Report</em>, quantifying &quot;every sequel invalidates how much early setting&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: extremely low</strong>. SSJ4 (GT) and Super Saiyan God (Super) are two completely incompatible transformation systems; Super&#39;s &quot;Zeno destroys universes&quot; and original&#39;s &quot;Supreme Kai sustains universe&quot; power structure directly conflict; Heroes&#39;s &quot;God Blue&quot; is pure game-style stacking; no law basis</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: extremely high (global sample-level)</strong>. Dragon Ball is &quot;successful IP forced to continue&quot; world&#39;s number-one negative textbook — original should have ended, commercial logic forcibly continued, result three works mutually eat, fans split, setting completely toy-ized</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</strong>. Every sequel defaults &quot;Goku has to come out and fight again&quot;; Goku alone carries forty years of IP life; civilizational institutional construction zero</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: three works repeatedly develop same protagonist; creative resources severe internal friction</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: villains repeatedly pulled back, nostalgia repeatedly consumed; story completeness plundered</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo system at least self-consistent within one book; Dragon Ball three works mutually retcon</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad Ranks across three timelines die their own deaths; no cross-line institutional guarantee</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: timelines should be multiverse&#39;s rich ore, but written into mutually contradictory toy boxes</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball&#39;s retcon is not Toriyama alone&#39;s fault; it is &quot;successful IP must continue&quot; commercial structural disease. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is the law-first axiom: work ended is ended; sequels via appendix increment, do not overturn old setting; truly want to expand multiverse, then legislate first &quot;which timeline counts.&quot; Dragon Ball&#39;s three-works-mutually-eat tells all long-form creators — without legislating law, however great an IP will be eaten by itself in sequels.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · retcon-ending deep analysis · GT/Super/Heroes multi-line contradictions described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./432_模块2-龙珠-总论悟空与战力膨胀体系定性.html">Entry 432 · Overview</a> · <a href="./438_模块2-龙珠-剧情绑架设定案例-为剧情强行变身的典型.html">Entry 438 · Plot-Kidnapping Case</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/27-锚点校准与维护.html">27-Anchor Calibration and Maintenance</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=i(a,[["render",s]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
